        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Athanasius of Alexandria",
        "Athanasius of Alexandria (350).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Athanasius of Alexandria</strong> <em>Orationes contra Arianos II.61</em> <small>(c. 350 AD)</small><p>&#x27;For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren&#x27; — Athanasius marks prōtotokon en pollois adelphois (firstborn among many brethren) as a SECOND prōtotokos-usage (paired with Col 1:15 prōtotokos pasēs ktiseōs and Heb 1:6 prōtotokos eis tēn oikoumenēn) — together demonstrating that &#x27;firstborn&#x27; consistently names ECONOMIC-HEADSHIP, not creaturely-priority. Among-many-brethren — the Son&#x27;s-incarnate-humanity makes him the elder-brother of the redeemed-human-race. The conformity to the Son&#x27;s-image is theosis from another angle: image-restoration + filial-incorporation. Tewahedo brotherhood-of-believers ecclesiology cites Rom 8:29 + Heb 2:11 as the prōtotokos-elder-brother pair.</p></aside>',
        "Athanasius of Alexandria, Orationes contra Arianos (Four Discourses Against the Arians, I-IV), in Select Writings and Letters of Athanasius, Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers (NPNF), Series 2, Vol. 4, ed. Archibald Robertson (Oxford / T&T Clark, 1892). PD. Greek text in Migne PG 26 (1857).",
